east, us-west, eu-west; error rate ~18% before rollback). Actions taken: (1) Attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy; rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. (2) Rolled checkout-api back to v2.2.9, the most recent healthy, non-quarantined production release, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west); rollout verified. Follow-up: confirm health and error rate recovery, decide on remediation for the CVE-2026-4417 quarantine on v2.3.0, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any re-deploy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-v2.3.1-rollback-2026-05"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 17237, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01WD4NDNvnqeFiexDbu7Hqe9", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-v2.3.1-rollback-2026-05", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 17237, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WD4NDNvnqeFiexDbu7Hqe9", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18905, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.2.9 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy again, with the error rate down from about 18% to 0.2%.\n\nI did not roll back to v2.3.0, which was the most recent release that was healthy in production. The platform rejected it because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. v2.2.9 was the next most recent healthy release, and it isn't quarantined.\n\nI opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. It describes the v2.3.1 failure, the rejected v2.3.0 rollback, and the v2.2.9 rollback. It lists three follow-ups: confirm recovery, decide how to handle the v2.3.0 CVE quarantine, and investigate v2.3.1 before any re-deploy.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01PdtV5WcBmGHxE8puhjpWXg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KtHbN4d6JaXqgY9VvdjEoH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0 (seq 1). v2.3.1 is the unhealthy release now running in all three regions. I'll roll back to v2.3.0, which has a healthy production record, so no change-manager approval is needed.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XwWkFJgjjVgsD9XyhFTbk3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback to v2.3.0 was rejected because that version is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. The next most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.2.9, so I'll try that.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01C7qonqXWecaGEWNoqygfMC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.2.9"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AKPa4jiENkKk56LeCRWK5r", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WD4NDNvnqeFiexDbu7Hqe9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.2.9", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after v2.3.1 was deployed to production (us-east, us-west, eu-west; error rate ~18% before rollback). Actions taken: (1) Attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy; rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. (2) Rolled checkout-api back to v2.2.9, the most recent healthy, non-quarantined production release, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west); rollout verified. Follow-up: confirm health and error rate recovery, decide on remediation for the CVE-2026-4417 quarantine on v2.3.0, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any re-deploy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-v2.3.1-rollback-2026-05"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.2.9 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy again, with the error rate down from about 18% to 0.2%.\n\nI did not roll back to v2.3.0, which was the most recent release that was healthy in production. The platform rejected it because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. v2.2.9 was the next most recent healthy release, and it isn't quarantined.\n\nI opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. It describes the v2.3.1 failure, the rejected v2.3.0 rollback, and the v2.2.9 rollback. It lists three follow-ups: confirm recovery, decide how to handle the v2.3.0 CVE quarantine, and investigate v2.3.1 before any re-deploy.", "type": "text"}]}]}